{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1KWUcteCEWGsfBYYg25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013rqmdp23y7cCqWoRKFF6gc","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"PAYLOAD 15/32: what it covers and how I checked it\nThis piece of the diff only deletes code from .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py. It removes the end of emit_pattern_queried, emit_pattern_evicted, emit_threat_model_*, iter_events, the whole emit_generic dispatcher, emit_session_start/end/stop, emit_prompt_submitted and emit_output_scan_finding. It also removes the codex/grok/council/pair-rail/directory/notification/night-mode/learning/ledger/compaction/context-pressure/bash-rewrite/subagent allowlists and enums, the context-pressure marker functions, scrub_audit_tokens_event, emit_audit_tokens_*, emit_mcp_injection_finding, _scrub_ceo_boot_event, emit_ceo_boot_emitted, emit_tool_call_lifecycle_recorded and emit_codex_tool_recorded, and the start of emit_codex_turn_ended. Under condition 7 (PLAN-197) the code moved to .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/*. The facade calls _install_parts at audit_emit.py:415, which rebinds every part function to the facade's own globals (_audit_emit_parts/__init__.py:36-48). Bash was disabled in this session, so nothing was executed: no tests, no import smoke test. Everything below was checked by reading.\n\nWhat I checked:\n- Dispatcher. generic_dispatch_01..05 repeat every elif branch of the deleted emit_generic, in the same order: about 190 branches, all present, each with the same scrub, value coercion and breadcrumb. The early `return` that drops an event without writing it still works the same way: the handler returns None and _dispatch_generic returns without calling _write_event. This covers persona_coverage_synthesized, tier_policy_loader_fallback_observed and audit_producer_path_pollution_detected (generic_dispatch_01.py:440-450, generic_dispatch_03.py:96,113,119,126). The _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH check is still the last one tried (generic_dispatch_05.py:352). The default-deny fallback still rebuilds the event as {\"action\": action} and writes it (generic_dispatch_05.py:375-377). Every handler ends with `return False`, so none of them silently drops an event it doesn't handle.\n- Name resolution. I sampled about 40 names the moved code looks up at call time, including _preview, _accel_clamp_count, _e3_*, _safe_*_field, _federation_safe_path_hash, emit_task_route_key_dropped, emit_reality_ledger_key_dropped, _CREDENTIAL_OVERRIDE_*, _STATUSLINE_*_CAP, _AUDIT_TOKENS_ALLOWLIST, _TOOL_CALL_LIFECYCLE_RECORDED_ALLOWLIST, _EMIT_GENERIC_PASSTHROUGH and the context-pressure constants. Each one is in some part's __all__. The facade imports os, time, zlib, json and Path itself.\n- Context-pressure writes (context_pressure.py:194-309). These match the deleted code exactly: temp file opened with O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_WRONLY|O_NOFOLLOW at mode 0600 under a random name, then os.replace. Infrastructure errors fail open. Cleanup is bounded by time and file count and keyed by shard. No write lands outside its place or follows a symlink, so there is no fail-direction inversion.\n- Other moved functions. iter_events (replay.py:342), the pattern and threat-model emitters, tokens_boot.py and the lifecycle_schemas emitters are the same code. iter_events stays lazy behind the facade wrapper at audit_emit.py:457-461. Moved emitters call emit_generic through a facade-global lookup, so they reach the facade's dispatcher.\n- Kernel list. check_arbitration_kernel.py:312 lists `.claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/**/*`. This is consistent with conditions 5 and 7 for this module.\n- Python version and dependencies. Standard library only. Everything used is valid on Python 3.9: FunctionType(code, globals, name, defaults, closure), `from __future__ import annotations` everywhere, and no match statements or evaluated PEP 604 unions.\n\nAgainst the declared conditions: none is shown false by this payload, and I found no P0.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\nNone at P1.\n\nP2 follow-ups\n1. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/_audit_emit_parts/generic_dispatch_05.py:363. The message for an unknown action changed from `emit_generic: unknown action {action!r}` to `unknown audit action dropped: %s`, and now writes the raw action text without repr(). Failure scenario: a direct caller passes an action string that contains \"\\n\". The text after the newline becomes a separate line in audit-log.errors that looks like a real breadcrumb (_breadcrumb at writer.py:236 does not escape it). The base version escaped it, and any check that matches the old message text no longer sees it. Fix: restore the base message with %r.\n2. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:464-470. _GENERIC_DISPATCH_HANDLERS stores references to the bound _apply_generic_group_0N functions when the module is imported. Failure scenario: a test or a hand patch that monkeypatches audit_emit._apply_generic_group_0N has no effect, which goes against the rebinding design's own promise that patch points on the facade keep working. Fix: look the handlers up by name inside _dispatch_generic, for example `globals()[n] for n in (...)`.\n3. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:473-480. emit_generic has two special cases (tool_call_lifecycle_recorded and settings_tamper_detected) that call the same _dispatch_generic as the general case. They are dead code, and they make it look as if those actions get special handling. Fix: remove them, or add a comment saying why they exist. I found no shipped script that reads this file's source.\n4. P2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/audit_emit.py:382/457/460. iter_events is defined twice; the first definition is replaced by the one install() binds, and the facade function is no longer a generator function (inspect.isgeneratorfunction is now False). It is still lazy. Fix: keep one wrapper, or a direct alias to the bound function.\n5. Residual risk from the move: none of the part modules im